      <div class="cnote" style="margin-top:8px;">This uses a simple compound growth model and does not account for taxes, exchange fees, or Bitcoin's extreme volatility. Historical Bitcoin CAGR from 2015 to 2024 was approximately 50% — but includes multiple 80%+ drawdowns. A 20% annual return assumption is conservative relative to history but aggressive relative to traditional assets. Past performance is not predictive.</div>
